    "lineage": "Compression lineage, the SUPERSEDED DESIGN: compact (Colin McMaster, 1980; shipped in 4.xBSD ucb/) used Gallager's adaptive Huffman coding -- one-pass, no table transmitted, but slow and ~38% savings. compress (Thomas et al. 1984, LZW) beat it decisively on speed and ratio, then LZW's Unisys patent pressure produced gzip/DEFLATE (1992-93). Preserved from the unix-history-repo at tag BSD-4_2 (ucb/compact: compact.c, uncompact.c, tree.c, compact.h, Makefile, ccat.sh)."
